zerops:index/serviceSubdomainAccess:Serv.description:
Enables Zerops-generated HTTP subdomains for an already deployed service. Declare an explicit dependency on the deployment that defines HTTP ports. Disabling access does not stop the service.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as std from "@pulumi/std";
import * as zerops from "@pulumi/zerops";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
// Existing runtime service ID.
const serviceId = config.require("serviceId");
const app = new zerops.ServiceDeploy("app", {
    serviceId: serviceId,
    archivePath: "./app.tar.gz",
    zeropsYaml: std.file({
        input: "./zerops.yml",
    }).then(invoke => invoke.result),
    setup: "app",
});
// The deployment must declare an HTTP port (for example TCP/HTTP 3000).
// A service_id reference alone does not establish deployment ordering.
const appServiceSubdomainAccess = new zerops.ServiceSubdomainAccess("app", {serviceId: serviceId}, {
    dependsOn: [app],
});
export const urls = appServiceSubdomainAccess.urls;
```
